    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0637" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.5211/517</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Protocol
                        and Conferences</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Southgate</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-10">October 10, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the conclusion of his conversation with the Spanish Ambassador<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d483-f1"/> the Secretary referred to the conversation recently held
                    between Mr. Dunn and Mr. de la Casa with reference to a speech made by Mr.
                    Gibernau of the Spanish Embassy. The Secretary stated that <pb facs="0638"
                        n="539" xml:id="pg539"/> apparently what Mr. Dunn had said had been
                    misunderstood and that there was no intention whatsoever on the part of the
                    Department to make any statement which could be construed as restricting the
                    freedom of speech of members of foreign Missions on subjects of general interest
                    concerning their own countries.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
